{"id": "EUVD-2026-82076", "enisaUuid": "72443ffa-e71b-3da0-895c-eb700fd0754e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/cxgb4: free STAG index when TPT entry write fails\n\nwrite_tpt_entry() allocates a new STAG index with c4iw_get_resource() and\nbumps stats.stag.cur before programming the entry.  When\nwrite_adapter_mem() fails, it returns the error without releasing the index\nor reversing the statistic.  No MR is inserted into rhp->mrs, so\nderegistration never reclaims it, leaking the index until device teardown.\n\nRecord whether this call allocated the index and, on a failed write, return\nit to tpt_table and decrement stats.stag.cur.  Key the rollback on both the\nwrite error and that flag, not the error alone: a non-reset update carries\na caller-owned STAG that this call did not allocate and must not free.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:03:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fe4731bfbd8d83c4a14b4af3a27329969ce8a99", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f6976d635d190e3d7af7103daaa581cf1ccc12e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9eeafcda1d6c11f0eec532243c4e96ec8c632bd7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a21e5114cec4cd3f8a2843d4c46bc49634d6e96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f17ca7ab5269ac2504e1039c3921373dccd7712", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2e37d1ab773be3cd26b1c19593ca2dbcece9c57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a64e2beb450179a5d43034af8d5476a11eac1486", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fdfb5cea4bf070cdb31d997efd87bb684df041fd"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v598-vrqp-g6vj", "CVE-2026-90415"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "010b113c-260d-390e-af92-1ad2abbf6d2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "49eef126-7927-30d8-8420-534f74d820ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec3eead217181d7360a11317a888ceb30807867c <5a21e5114cec4cd3f8a2843d4c46bc49634d6e96"}, {"id": "55c40a4e-c502-3967-a9c8-2ed2561b0724", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec3eead217181d7360a11317a888ceb30807867c <2f17ca7ab5269ac2504e1039c3921373dccd7712"}, {"id": "5a8031e5-420b-3220-bebc-3a139fe1b21b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.5"}, {"id": "5eff4763-dd1d-3c35-b7d8-152b5f5398be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "643fbcf5-7586-336f-9eed-077e35c206d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6e651a5c-31f2-3a53-85f5-6ff046946e50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "7c0bd6a3-deb4-3960-96c6-4d8e198b29b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "7ffaad17-a948-3506-85ff-f039a6b6c424", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec3eead217181d7360a11317a888ceb30807867c <5fe4731bfbd8d83c4a14b4af3a27329969ce8a99"}, {"id": "8527616f-7754-3c6f-a5ef-c497ccc77ad7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "9793cbdd-73d0-34d5-a0ae-ef42086d204c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec3eead217181d7360a11317a888ceb30807867c <fdfb5cea4bf070cdb31d997efd87bb684df041fd"}, {"id": "a9296465-eafd-3159-a346-64dbcc37760b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec3eead217181d7360a11317a888ceb30807867c <9eeafcda1d6c11f0eec532243c4e96ec8c632bd7"}, {"id": "ad95587b-ad40-3c53-9baa-c037f28a86a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec3eead217181d7360a11317a888ceb30807867c <a2e37d1ab773be3cd26b1c19593ca2dbcece9c57"}, {"id": "d7f81add-c59e-3342-bae2